# Title: Potentially Suspicious Command Executed Via Run Dialog Box - Registry
# ID: a7df0e9e-91a5-459a-a003-4cde67c2ff5d
# Status: test
# Level: high
# Author: Ahmed Farouk, Nasreddine Bencherchali
# Date: 2024-11-01
# Tags: attack.execution, attack.t1059.001
# Description: Detects execution of commands via the run dialog box on Windows by checking values of the "RunMRU" registry key.
# This technique was seen being abused by threat actors to deceive users into pasting and executing malicious commands, often disguised as CAPTCHA verification steps.
# Converted by: Sigma Universal SIEM/EDR CLI

((TargetObject CONTAIN "\\Microsoft\\Windows\\CurrentVersion\\Explorer\\RunMRU") AND ((((Details CONTAIN "powershell" OR Details CONTAIN "pwsh")) AND ((Details CONTAIN " -e " OR Details CONTAIN " -ec " OR Details CONTAIN " -en " OR Details CONTAIN " -enc " OR Details CONTAIN " -enco" OR Details CONTAIN "ftp" OR Details CONTAIN "Hidden" OR Details CONTAIN "http" OR Details CONTAIN "iex" OR Details CONTAIN "Invoke-"))) OR ((Details CONTAIN "wmic") AND ((Details CONTAIN "shadowcopy" OR Details CONTAIN "process call create")))))
